{"type":"event","recovered":"Agent.messages.list","event":{"type":"tool_call","agent_id":"agent-69db0ac0-236d-41be-bc50-dcb357ce6281","run_id":"run-70711418-b45c-4fbf-958a-59c5ceb4412e","call_id":"tool_d5a3bc8d-ae92-40bc-9f48-32c34e0e722","name":"webSearch","args":{"searchTerm":"IANA example domain RFC 2606"},"status":"completed","result":{"status":"success","value":{"references":[{"title":"Web search results","url":"","chunk":"Links:\n1. [RFC 2606 - Reserved Top Level DNS Names](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc2606)\n2. [RFC 2606: Reserved Top Level DNS Names | RFC Editor](https://www.rfc-editor.org/info/rfc2606/)\n3. [IANA-managed Reserved Domains](https://www.iana.org/domains/reserved)\n4. [Example Domains](https://www.iana.org/help/example-domains)\n5. [](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6761.html)\n\nSynthesis:\nRFC 2606 reserves.test,.example,.invalid, and.localhost, plus example.com, example.net, example.org and all names beneath them, for testing, invalid names, local host use, or documentation [1][2]. IANA says example domains are not available for registration or transfer [3][4]. RFC 6761 clarifies that example names should generally resolve normally; software and DNS servers should not treat them specially, unlike.invalid, whose names are defined as nonexistent [5][6][7].\n\nHighlights:\n<result id=\"1\">\n<title>RFC 2606 - Reserved Top Level DNS Names</title>\n<url>https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc2606</url>\n<content>domain names are ... for use in private\n...\nTo safely satisfy these needs, four domain names are reserved as\n   listed and described below.\n...\n.test\n                .example\n                .invalid\n              .localhost\n...\n\".test\" is recommended for use in testing of current or new DNS\n      related code.\n...\nrecommended for use ... or as examples\n...\n3. Reserved Example Second Level Domain Names\n\n   The Internet Assigned Numbers Authority (IANA) also currently has the\n   following second level domain names reserved which can be used as\n   examples.\n...\n```\nRFC 2606              Reserved Top Level DNS Names             June 1999\n\n        example.com\n        example.net\n        example.org\n\n4. IANA Considerations\n\n   IANA has agreed to the four top level domain name reservations\n   specified in this document and will reserve them for the uses\n   indicated.</content>\n</result>\n\n<result id=\"2\">\n<title>RFC 2606: Reserved Top Level DNS Names | RFC Editor</title>\n<url>https://www.rfc-editor.org/info/rfc2606/</url>\n<content>test\n                .\n...\n3. Reserved Example Second Level Domain Names\n\n   The Internet Assigned Numbers Authority (IANA) also currently has the\n   following second level domain names reserved which can be used as\n   examples.\n...\n```\n\nRFC 2606              Reserved Top Level DNS Names             June 1999\n\n        example.com\n        example.net\n        example.org\n\n4. IANA Considerations\n\n   IANA has agreed to the four top level domain name reservations\n   specified in this document and will reserve them for the uses\n   indicated.</content>\n</result>\n\n<result id=\"3\">\n<title>IANA-managed Reserved Domains</title>\n<url>https://www.iana.org/domains/reserved</url>\n<content>## Example domains\n\nAs described in RFC 2606 and RFC 6761, a number of domains such as example.com and example.org are maintained for documentation purposes. These domains may be used as illustrative examples in documents without prior coordination with us. They are not available for registration or transfer.</content>\n</result>\n\n<result id=\"4\">\n<title>Example Domains</title>\n<url>https://www.iana.org/help/example-domains</url>\n<content>Example Domains\n\n# Example Domains\n\nAs described in RFC 2606 and RFC 6761, a number of domains such as example.com and example.org are maintained for documentation purposes. These domains may be used as illustrative examples in documents without prior coordination with us. They are not available for registration or transfer.\n\nWe provide a web service on the example domain hosts to provide basic information on the purpose of the domain. These web services are provided as best effort, but are not designed to support production applications. While incidental traffic for incorrectly configured applications is expected, please do not design applications that require the example domains to have operating HTTP service.\n\n## Further Reading\n\nLast revised 2017-05-13.</content>\n</result>\n\n<result id=\"5\">\n<title></title>\n<url>https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6761.html</url>\n<content>Analogous to Special-Use IPv4 Addresses [RFC5735], the Domain Name\n   System (DNS) [RFC1034][RFC1035] has its own concept of reserved\n   names, such as \"example.com.\", \"example.net.\", and \"example.org.\", or\n   any name falling under the top-level pseudo-domain \"invalid.\"\n   [RFC2606].  However, \"Reserved Top Level DNS Names\" [RFC2606] does\n   not state whether implementations are expected to treat such names\n   differently, and if so, in what way.\n...\n6.  Initial Registry\n\n   The initial IANA \"Special-Use Domain Names\" registry shall contain\n   entries for the private-address [RFC1918] reverse-mapping domains and\n   for the existing Reserved Top Level DNS Names [RFC2606].\n...\n6.5.  Domain Name Reservation Considerations for Example Domains\n\n   The domains \"example.\", \"example.com.\", \"example.net.\",\n   \"example.org.\", and any names falling within those domains, are\n   special in the following ways:\n\n   1.  Users SHOULD understand that example names are reserved for use\n       in documentation.\n...\n7.  DNS Registries/Registrars MUST NOT grant requests to register\n       example names in ... normal way to any person or entity.  All\n...\nexample names are registered in perpetuity to IANA:\n...\nDomain Name: EXAMPLE.COM\n        Registrar: RESERVED-INTERNET ASSIGNED NUMBERS AUTHORITY\n        Whois Server: whois.iana.org\n        Referral URL: http://res-dom.iana.org\n        Name Server: A.IANA-SERVERS.NET\n        Name Server: B.IANA-SERVERS.NET\n        Status: clientDeleteProhibited\n        Status: clientTransferProhibited\n        Status: clientUpdateProhibited\n        Updated Date: 26-mar-2004\n        Creation Date: 14-aug-1995\n        Expiration Date: 13-aug-2011\n\n   IANA currently maintains a web server providing a web page explaining\n...\nUse Domain Names\n...\npopulated with the ... -address reverse\n...\nand the Reserved Top Level DNS Names outlined above in Section 6.\n...\nNames\", BCP 32, RFC ... 606, June 1999.</content>\n</result>"},{"title":"","url":"https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6761.html","chunk":"Full page text written to file: /home/ubuntu/.cursor/projects/tmp-csdk-ws/agent-tools/b2b96879-e71c-486e-adde-76d76c91de30.txt\nSize: 28.2 KB, 654 lines\nUse shell / grep / read_file on this path to inspect the page; no follow-up fetch is needed."}]}},"started_at_ms":1790444242461,"completed_at_ms":1790444246503}}
